{"id":"f8cdda6985c34f12","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-csabaian.md","title":"Relative Geometrization Certificate","display":"thm-csabaian — Relative Geometrization Certificate","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-csabaian","aliases":["58-thm-csabaian"],"display":"thm-csabaian — Relative Geometrization Certificate","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-jsj-decomposition.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-thurston-geometry.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-csabaian"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-csabaian</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-csabaian — Relative Geometrization Certificate"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ff113b4d11bbe470\" href=\"?note=ff113b4d11bbe470\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-jsj-decomposition.md\">../batch11/58-df-jsj-decomposition.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"230b6c3bb3938a47\" href=\"?note=230b6c3bb3938a47\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-thurston-geometry.md\">../batch09/58-df-thurston-geometry.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal A,E\\in V\">\\(M,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal A,E\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle\">\\(\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle\\)</span> is a set-coded decomposition certificate.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal A\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal A\\in V\\)</span> is a supplied relation whose pairs <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle N,G\\rangle\">\\(\\langle N,G\\rangle\\)</span> certify that piece <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\">\\(N\\)</span> admits model geometry <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V\">\\(S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V\\)</span> are the eight standard geometry labels.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are from the cited dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}geometrization\\text{-}certificate}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet,\nS^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S(M,\\mathcal T)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(N_\\bullet,n,\\operatorname{ran}(N_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(G_\\bullet,n,E)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S\n(E,S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle N_\\bullet(i),G_\\bullet(i)\\rangle\\in\\mathcal A\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}geometrization\\text{-}certificate}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet,\nS^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S(M,\\mathcal T)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(N_\\bullet,n,\\operatorname{ran}(N_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(G_\\bullet,n,E)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S\n(E,S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle N_\\bullet(i),G_\\bullet(i)\\rangle\\in\\mathcal A\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}csabaian\\text{-}certificate\\text{-}projection}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\n\\to\n\\forall i\\in\\pi_1(\\mathcal C)\\;\n\\bigl\\langle\\pi_2(\\mathcal C)(i),\\pi_3(\\mathcal C)(i)\\bigr\\rangle\n\\in\\mathcal A.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}csabaian\\text{-}certificate\\text{-}projection}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\n\\to\n\\forall i\\in\\pi_1(\\mathcal C)\\;\n\\bigl\\langle\\pi_2(\\mathcal C)(i),\\pi_3(\\mathcal C)(i)\\bigr\\rangle\n\\in\\mathcal A.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The standard name is the Thurston–Perelman geometrization theorem; “Csabaian” is retained only in the filename.</li>\n<li>This atom now records exactly what the current library can set-code: a JSJ family, a finite piece enumeration, one of the eight registered geometry labels for each piece, and an explicit admission relation.</li>\n<li>The actual existence theorem is not asserted until upstream atoms define closed connected orientable smooth three-manifolds, extract the pieces of a prime-plus-JSJ decomposition, and certify that a piece admits a model geometry. The former file silently postulated all three missing notions.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Thurston, Three-Dimensional Geometry and Topology</li>\n<li>Perelman, Ricci flow with surgery on three-manifolds</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-jsj-decomposition.md","status":"resolved","id":"ff113b4d11bbe470","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-jsj-decomposition.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-thurston-geometry.md","status":"resolved","id":"230b6c3bb3938a47","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-thurston-geometry.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal A,E\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\langle N,G\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"N","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}geometrization\\text{-}certificate}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\exists\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet,\nS^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathcal C=\\langle\\mathcal T,n,N_\\bullet,G_\\bullet\\rangle\\\\\n&{}\\land n\\in\\omega\n\\land\\operatorname{JSJDecomposition}_S(M,\\mathcal T)\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(N_\\bullet,n,\\operatorname{ran}(N_\\bullet))\n\\land\\mathrm{Function}(G_\\bullet,n,E)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{EightThurstonGeometries}_S\n(E,S^3,\\mathbb R^3,\\mathbb H^3,S^2\\times\\mathbb R,\n\\mathbb H^2\\times\\mathbb R,\\widetilde{\\mathrm{SL}}_2(\\mathbb R),\n\\mathrm{Nil},\\mathrm{Sol})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle N_\\bullet(i),G_\\bullet(i)\\rangle\\in\\mathcal A\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}csabaian\\text{-}certificate\\text{-}projection}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{GeometrizationCertificate}_S(\\mathcal C,M,\\mathcal A,E)\n\\to\n\\forall i\\in\\pi_1(\\mathcal C)\\;\n\\bigl\\langle\\pi_2(\\mathcal C)(i),\\pi_3(\\mathcal C)(i)\\bigr\\rangle\n\\in\\mathcal A.","display":true}],"bytes":2978,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4104","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-thm-csabaian.md|58-thm-csabaian]]（batch10）"}],"outgoing":["ff113b4d11bbe470","230b6c3bb3938a47","36d7463d215be751"]}